\f1\fs22 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In the middle of the night, Sarah\'92s tablet erupted with her boss\'92s ringtone\'97a custom commission that somehow blended elevator music, the sound of coins tumbling into a collection plate, and, if you listened closely, a muttered threat of redundancy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She ignored it for six minutes, but the latest update to Persistence Plus\'99 had just activated Phase Three: Guilt Harmonics.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>On screen, the name: 
\f2\i Roderick Ashby-Prynne
\f1\i0 , which sounded every bit the third son of a Viscount forced to manage money for people with a less congenital nose.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah!\'94 he boomed. \'93My little absentee! How\'92s the old blast radius healing? Still glowing?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Like Chernobyl in a cocktail dress,\'94 Sarah croaked, eyeing the antique holoscreen Nancy had parked in the corner, on a curvaceous \'9250s accent chair, all white vinyl and gold piping, built for someone determined to lounge, preen, or faint with style. It hadn\'92t twitched since it was uprooted from her office.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Splendid!\'94 Ashby-Prynne continued, voice dripping with ancestral entitlement. \'93Tell me, what are you wearing?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I imagine at this time of night, you\'92re in a skimpy little neglig\'e9?\'94 Sarah could hear him try to pronounce 
\f2\i neglig\'e9 
\f1\i0 with the correct amount of French sauciness.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I beg your pardon?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Is it black, or white? Or perhaps red, or purple?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93White,\'94 Sarah answered hurriedly, motivated by her need to deny she\'92d ever wear purple to bed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Of course it is, of course it is,\'94 Ashby-Prynne encouraged salaciously. \'93Listen, poppet\'97can I call you poppet? Never mind, I already have. The office is feral without you. Jenkins from Accounts has been forced to look at his wife\'92s photo. The same woman, Sarah, three days running. Market confidence is in free-fall.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah, shifting on the bed, gave her cramps a chance to upgrade from \'93acute\'94 to \'93zealous tissue damage.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He should try pornography,\'94 she said through clenched teeth. \'93I hear it\'92s more interactive these days.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Not the point, darling. Did you get my notes on last Tuesday\'92s Lateral Bounce Metrics? Dreadful absence. Who can we rely on for in-person bounce projections if not for you? Stephanie from Marketing tried, but maternity ruins motivation for metrics. The algorithm flagged her immediately.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Bounce Metrics?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Perfectly science-based. Part of our new Kinetic Performance Initiative\'97People & Culture assures us it\'92s completely legal if we spell \'91metrics\'92 without vowels. You should see the curves. The graphs are fantastic, too.\'94 He wheezed an aristocratic laugh, like a bishop passing a stone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Roderick, I was in an explosion. With fire, collapse, and an unfriendly introduction to my own blood.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, yes\'97heroic, but you\'92ve been happily presenting at the office since then for weeks.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Part time. And now\'85 well, I\'92m quite ill.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We\'92d miss you at tomorrow\'92s company no-bra volleyball,\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah eyed the holoscreen\'92s shining blankness, her body held together by spite, tape, and second thoughts. \'93I can barely stand, Roderick.\'94 Calling him 
\f2\i The Rod
\f1\i0 , as expected, was completely out of the question.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Well, okay,\'94 Ashby-Prynne said with reserved disappointment. \'93Perhaps we can make exception this once. But you did miss Wet Blouse Wednesday. We\'92re assessing how moisture impacts workplace unlock rates. Jenkins brought in a Super Soaker. Very team-forward.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93That\'92s sexual harassment, Roderick.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, no, that\'92s corporate hydration. Legal signed off. Well, Jackson-Snape from Legal signed off, but what is a cousin for?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good night, Roderick,\'94 Sarah said and hung up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She closed her eyes and practiced her Monday smile. A rictus that was less \'93bright-eyed and bushy-tailed,\'94 more \'93planning which parts of you to feed the office shredder.\'94 But then again, Ashby-Prynne probably authored the original employee manual, \'93Grin and Bare It,\'94 and found the legal settlement the real thrill.
